# statusgen pin for the adopter-scaffold example.
#
# This is the file an adopting repo commits so its CI (and a local install) can
# fetch a KNOWN statusgen binary and verify it byte-for-byte before running it.
# A pinned sha256 is the one thing a re-tagged release cannot silently swap out.
#
# Format: <artifact> <tag> <sha256>
#   - <artifact> field 1 carries the component; a bare `statusgen` line is what
#     CI selects with `grep '^statusgen '` (trailing space, never matching a
#     `statusgen-<platform>` line) and always wants linux-amd64.
#   - <tag> is the plain repo-level semver tag this public `assay` release home
#     cuts (`v0.26.0`), NOT a component-prefixed `statusgen/vX.Y.Z`.
#   - <sha256> is harvested from the PUBLISHED release's checksums.txt, never a
#     local build (a local build lacks the release -ldflags stamp and hashes
#     differently).
#
# Per-platform lines below carry the same three-field shape; a local install
# selects by DETECTED platform and needs a committed hash for each one.
